From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Duran <15650777+carlos-duran@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] BananaDS: Auto has no Disconnect and no Players row; Off
 leaves, Auto hosts with Host's size

The LAN page's Disconnect in Auto paused Auto until the game's wifi had been
off for 3 s and on again. Mario Kart DS turns it off for less than that when
you leave its multiplayer menu for the main menu and come straight back, so
Auto stayed paused and didn't look for hosts. Any wifi off can't lift the
pause either: the logs show that a duration can't tell its "Create group"
(wifi off for 3 s or more, still in its multiplayer menu) from the main menu
and straight back (under 3 s), so Disconnect would be undone inside
multiplayer. To leave on purpose in Auto, pick Off: the session ends or is
left at once (the others hear it, melonDS patch 0097), and Auto again starts
afresh. Host and Join keep their Disconnect.

- Auto's Disconnect and its pause ("hold") are gone. In a local wireless
  game Auto's Mode row offers Off only, asked first, as a Disconnect is.
- The menu's requests are kept in order and all carried out: Off then Auto
  before the emulator's thread gets to them still ends the session first
  (the latest alone, Auto, already on, would have kept the old session).
- Held is left for a problem only (UDP 7063 or 7064 taken): the page says
  it and that Auto tries again when the game's wifi goes off for 3 s and on,
  or on Off then Auto.
- No "Players (if hosting)" row: a session Auto hosts has Host's size
  (wifi.local_players, 4 by default, 2-16), set by Host's Players row; the
  page no longer saves a size for Auto, and Auto's resize while alone is
  gone. The page shows a joined session's size as the host's.

Test knob: wifi.local_test_mode = <mode>@<frame>, the Mode row by frame.
